{"kind":"assert","text":"PB-3, after gate END b2f3f7fb (failed): Hugh wants PB-3 to unblock live application use, so it goes next in the gate slot, ahead of the LL-1 source. The failure is a real product fault from PB-3's own change: ReadSessions keeps a workerd AbortController made in one request context and aborts it from ReadSessions.forget in another. Workerd refuses that across Durable Object contexts. The hosted.scope test is a deterministic red, so it is the named red.\nConditions:\n1. Do not keep any request-scoped I/O object (AbortController, stream, promise resolver) beyond its context. Have forget signal the open stream in a way the stream's own context consumes, for example a plain flag or listener set that the stream checks and acts on in its own context. Use the shape you judge simplest, and name it in the review.\n2. Run packages/mcp/test/hosted.scope.test.ts alone, red before the fix and green after. Then run the whole Native stage alone before START.\n3. Then run a full gate on the new head. Native failed on product code, so the earlier stages' passes do not stand for the new head.\n4. The automatic renewal interval stays off until the LL-1 source lands. The watch and the enter, update and leave paths ship now.\nDO rate for the record: after the PB-2 deploy, dap-grow read 1,932 per hour (17:31 to 17:46 UTC), and 2,000 per hour from 01:00 to 01:15 UTC. dap-lending read 0 in both windows.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}